# Preserved audit evidence must survive a checkout byte-for-byte.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the authoring machine, so without this rule a fresh
# clone would rewrite these files LF -> CRLF in the working tree. The SHA-256
# hashes recorded in audits/*/MANIFEST.md would then fail for every person who
# tried to verify them, and the claim that the bytes are preserved would be
# false for everyone except the author.
audits/** -text
